{
  "description": "Reading the synced settings. `settings` is the merged view's `settings` map (shared/fixtures/merge.json); `expected` is what the client acts on. `feedSort`: one of newest (default), shortest, title, random (shared/fixtures/feed-order.json); oldest and longest, which older versions saved, read as the default like any other unknown value. `channelSort`: one of newest (default), name, unwatched (shared/fixtures/channel-order.json). `autoplay`: a boolean, default false. `timeChip`: one of none (default), day, week, month (shared/fixtures/feed-chips.json). `topicChips`: an array of strings, the selected topic chips' YouTube video category ids (shared/fixtures/feed-chips.json), default []; it is read as written, with no sorting or de-duplication, and ids that are in no table are kept here (the chips ignore them). `channelTimeChip` and `channelTopicChips`: the channel list's own time chip and topic chips (shared/fixtures/channel-chips.json), read exactly as `timeChip` and `topicChips` are and independent of them. `groupChips` and `channelGroupChips`: the selected group chips' names for the feed's row and for the channel list's row (shared/fixtures/groups.json), each an array of strings, default [], independent of each other; like the topic settings they are read as written, with no sorting, trimming or de-duplication, and names that are no existing group are kept here (the chips ignore them). A setting that is missing, or whose value is anything else (another string, another type, an array holding a non-string), reads as its default; the entry itself stays in the file untouched. Names not listed here are ignored. A change writes `{at: now, value}` under the setting's name in the device's own file, keeping any unknown fields the entry had.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "no settings: every default",
      "settings": {},
      "expected": {
        "feedSort": "newest",
        "channelSort": "newest",
        "autoplay": false,
        "timeChip": "none",
        "topicChips": [],
        "channelTimeChip": "none",
        "channelTopicChips": [],
        "groupChips": [],
        "channelGroupChips": []
      }
    },
